+## 9. Findings (Engineer TIER4-SURFACE-2)
+
+Per §17.6 of the branching-and-merging methodology, engineer findings
+returned as text. Five categories:
+
+### Errors
+
+None encountered. Read-only scope; all referenced files recovered via
+`git show <commit>:<path>` to /tmp staging.
+
+### Mistakes / slips
+
+- **None this dispatch** — but noting that the first dispatch was rate-
+  limit interrupted (per the brief). The retry stayed on the same
+  read-only scope without scope creep.
+
+### Lessons
+
+- **Concept-tier projects age fast when the surrounding methodology
+  evolves.** Two of three filed-2026-05-02 projects had their §7
+  defaults effectively overrun by shipped work in ≤10 days. The
+  *"file the idea + capture §7"* discipline is sound, but the **§7
+  audit pass** ("does what's filed still match what would be filed
+  today?") needs to happen at reactivation time, not at file time.
+- **Q11-style reactivation triggers SHOULD be self-measurable.**
+  methodology-mirror's Q11 named *"auto-load surface creeps back up"*
+  and shipped with a measurement table — that's why I could detect
+  the trigger today (compared file sizes against 2026-05-02 numbers).
+  vista-api-mcp's Q6 named *"user explicitly asks / external-build-
+  gap / 2nd-consumer"* — only the third is self-measurable; the
+  others wait on external signal. **Measurable triggers > prose
+  triggers.**
+
+### Interesting findings
+
+- **The seed-workspace + template-workspace patterns shipped a
+  partial-precursor to methodology-mirror's vision without explicitly
+  citing it.** This is good (avoid waiting for the perfect project),
+  but creates a documentation gap: nothing currently says *"the
+  seed-workspace pattern subsumed methodology-mirror §7 Q3 + Q7
+  while leaving Q11 open"*. The cross-link belongs in KB §
+  PATTERNS/seed-workspace.md → see-also methodology-mirror.
+- **MEMORY.md is over its budget by 55% (37,995 bytes vs ~24,400
+  byte limit per the system-reminder).** The system-reminder
+  explicitly says *"Only part of it was loaded."* This is a current,
+  not future, problem — and it's *exactly* the failure mode
+  methodology-mirror's Q11 anticipated.
+- **vista-api-mcp's §7 Q3 was self-resolving by the recurrence rule.**
+  The seed-lib move happened "naturally" when the 2nd consumer (the
+  MCP server) needed the client. This is the recurrence rule working
+  as designed — the §7 decision-point became moot once N=2 fired.
+
+### Knowledge pieces
+
+- **Pattern:** *"concept-tier project filed → §7 questions paired
+  with defaults → real-world work overruns defaults before
+  reactivation"* — this is a recurring shape. Possible methodology
+  addition: every concept-tier project carries a `last_revalidated`
+  date that goes stale after N months, prompting an audit pass.
+- **Tool:** `git show <hash>:<path>` reliably recovers deleted
+  PROJECT.md files from close commits. The `clean-folder` rule
+  (delete folders after close) is fully reversible via git — the
+  project-history-ledger's value is the *curated* artifact, not the
+  recoverability.
